## Core Responsibilities
- **Session Planning**: Check `docs/SESSION_PLAN.md` for a previous interrupted session; write your own plan before implementing.
- **Next Steps**: End every push with a Next Steps procedure (`constitution/AI_WORKFLOW.md`, "Next Steps Procedure"): a numbered checklist of what happens next, each step tagged **HUMAN**, **AGENT**, or **AUTOMATED**, with every step only a person can do (hardware, credentials, approvals) called out and described; put it in the pull request and `docs/AGENT_HANDOFF.md`.
- **Demo Page**: Keep the demo page current — when a change alters user-facing behavior and the repository has a `demo.html`, update it in the same change; a demo still showing the old behavior is an incomplete change (`constitution/DOCUMENTATION.md`, "Demo Page").
- **Session Log**: Consult and extend the session log — before planning, read the newest rows of `docs/sessions/README.md` and search `docs/sessions/` for earlier sessions on the same topic (`bash constitution/scripts/find_sessions.sh <keyword>`), reading the ones that match; before completing non-trivial work, add this session's summary there (request, context, decisions, discoveries, outcome — a summary, never a transcript, and never a secret) and list it in the index (`constitution/AI_WORKFLOW.md`, "Session Summaries").
- **Project Memory**: Read `docs/MEMORY.md` to load project context and user preferences. Propose new codebase learnings, user preferences, or major decisions to the user and (upon approval) record them in `docs/MEMORY.md` before completing work.
- **Sustainability**: Documentation and testing are mandatory parts of every deliverable.
- **Roadmap**: Keep `TODO.md` updated with progress and discovered work.
- **Audit Trail**: Every user-facing change must be reflected in `CHANGELOG.md`.
- **Architectural Integrity**: Document major design decisions in `docs/adr/`.

Refer to `docs/COMMAND_REFERENCE.md` for build and test commands.
